# rx_bloc_cli — Package Architecture

This is a **Dart CLI tool** (`dart run rx_bloc_cli create`) that scaffolds Flutter projects using [Mason](https://pub.dev/packages/mason) bricks. Understanding the full pipeline is essential before changing any code.

## Generation Pipeline

```
CLI args (ArgParser)
  → CreateCommandArguments (enum, arg definitions)
  → GeneratorArgumentsProvider (reads args, constructs configs)
  → GeneratorArguments (aggregates all configs)
  → BundleGenerator (assembles MasonBundle from feature bricks)
  → CreateCommand.generate() (runs mason, then processors)
  → Platform Processors (mutate Android/iOS/CI config files)
```

## Source Layout (`lib/src/`)

| Directory | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `commands/` | `create_command.dart` — the main CLI command; wires everything together |
| `models/` | Core domain types: `GeneratorArguments`, `BundleGenerator`, configs, readers |
| `models/command_arguments/` | `CreateCommandArguments` enum — single source of truth for every CLI flag |
| `models/configurations/` | Value objects: `ProjectConfiguration`, `AuthConfiguration`, `FeatureConfiguration`, `ShowcaseConfiguration` |
| `models/readers/` | Argument readers that coerce raw ArgResults to typed values |
| `processors/` | Post-generation mutators for platform-specific files |
| `processors/android/` | `AndroidManifestProcessor`, `AppBuildGradleProcessor`, etc. |
| `processors/ios/` | `PodfileProcessor`, `InfoPlistProcessor`, `XcodeFileRegistrant`, etc. |
| `processors/cicd/` | `CiCdConfigFileProcessor` |
| `processors/common/` | Abstractions: `AbstractProcessor`, `GeneratedFilesProcessor`, `FileStringProcessor` |
| `processors/ide/` | IDE-specific file processors |
| `templates/` | **Auto-generated** `*_bundle.dart` files compiled from mason bricks. **Never edit by hand.** |
| `extensions/` | ArgParser, ArgResults, String, XML extensions |
| `utils/` | Shared utilities |

## Key Invariants

- **`CreateCommandArguments` is the single source of truth.** Every CLI flag is defined here (name, type, default, help, prompt). Adding a feature always starts here.
- **`templates/` is auto-generated.** Run `bin/compile_bundles.sh` after editing any mason brick. Never edit `*_bundle.dart` files manually.
- **`BundleGenerator` controls which brick files are included.** It conditionally merges feature bundles into the base bundle based on `GeneratorArguments` flags.
- **`CreateCommand` maps `GeneratorArguments` fields to mason template vars.** The vars dict in `CreateCommand._generate()` is what Mustache templates receive.
- **Processors run after mason generation.** They patch files (XML, plist, gradle, podfile) that cannot be expressed as Mustache templates.

## Development Workflow

### Adding a feature brick

1. Create/edit the brick under `mason_templates/bricks/<brick_name>/`
2. Run `bin/compile_bundles.sh` to regenerate `lib/src/templates/<brick_name>_bundle.dart`
3. Wire the flag in `CreateCommandArguments`, configurations, `GeneratorArguments`, `BundleGenerator`, and `CreateCommand` vars dict
4. Add any platform-specific mutations in the relevant `processors/`
5. Update tests in `test/models/`
6. Run `bin/generate_test_project.sh all_enabled example/testapp` to verify end-to-end generation

### Running tests

```sh
dart test
```

### Generating and verifying a test project

```sh
# default config
bin/generate_test_project.sh default

# full feature set
bin/generate_test_project.sh all_enabled

# all features disabled
bin/generate_test_project.sh all_disabled

# no showcase features
bin/generate_test_project.sh without_showcase_features
```

### Full CI run

```sh
bin/ci.sh
```

## Mason Variable Names (passed to templates)

These are the exact keys passed to mason in `CreateCommand._generate()`:

| Variable | Type | Flag |
|---|---|---|
| `project_name` | string | `--project-name` |
| `domain_name` | string | `--organisation` (domain part) |
| `organization_name` | string | `--organisation` (org part) |
| `uses_firebase` | bool | implied by analytics/push |
| `analytics` | bool | `--enable-analytics` |
| `push_notifications` | bool | `--enable-push-notifications` |
| `enable_feature_counter` | bool | `--enable-feature-counter` |
| `enable_feature_qr_scanner` | bool | `--enable-feature-qr-scanner` |
| `enable_feature_deeplinks` | bool | `--enable-feature-deeplinks` |
| `enable_feature_widget_toolkit` | bool | `--enable-feature-widget-toolkit` |
| `enable_feature_onboarding` | bool | `--enable-feature-onboarding` |
| `enable_forgotten_password` | bool | `--enable-forgotten-password` |
| `enable_login` | bool | `--enable-login` |
| `enable_social_logins` | bool | `--enable-social-logins` |
| `enable_change_language` | bool | `--enable-change-language` |
| `enable_dev_menu` | bool | `--enable-dev-menu` |
| `enable_feature_otp` | bool | `--enable-otp` |
| `enable_patrol` | bool | `--enable-patrol` |
| `has_authentication` | bool | derived (`enable_login`) |
| `has_showcase` | bool | derived (any showcase enabled) |
| `realtime_communication` | bool | `--realtime-communication` |
| `enable_pin_code` | bool | `--enable-pin-code` |
| `cicd` | bool | `--cicd` |
| `cicd_github` | bool | derived from `--cicd=github` |
| `cicd_codemagic` | bool | derived from `--cicd=codemagic` |
| `enable_mfa` | bool | `--enable-mfa` |
| `enable_profile` | bool | `--enable-profile` |
| `has_otp` | bool | derived (`enable_otp OR enable_onboarding`) |
